 or logging out removes it.", "Books you save for offline: when you choose Read offline, the book's text, and its audio if you ask, are kept on your device until you remove them from the book's page.", "If you turn on Listen offline on a schedule for an audiobook, the app also keeps a small note of that choice (how many chapters, Wi-Fi only, whether to remove finished ones) with the books, and saves or removes chapters as you listen; it goes when you turn it off or the books are cleared.", "Next to them the app keeps a small note of which account's offline place this device holds (a random id, not your name or email), so the place can be freed from another device; it goes when the books do.", "Books you upload: once you've opened one, or searched your uploads by keywords, its text is kept on that device so it keeps working if your connection drops. It's removed when you delete the book or log out.", "Everything else, such as reader settings, playback speed, the demo household and uploads made in the demo, stays in the open tab only and is gone when you refresh or close it.", "Your library, reading progress, bookmarks, highlights, saved words, lists, Up next queue, ratings, reading time and pace, quiz scores, player settings, club activity and uploaded books are saved with your account on our servers (Supabase), not in browser cookies. The Privacy Policy says how we use them, and Account lets you download or delete them.", "Listening on a speaker or TV uses your browser's own Chromecast or AirPlay picker: it loads no script, sets no cookie and keeps nothing in your browser, and the speaker plays the recording straight from the Internet Archive."]}, {"heading": "What else your browser loads from other sites", "paragraphs": ["Some parts of LiteraryWorm load straight from other companies' servers, so your browser sends them requests, with your IP address, and they handle them under their own policies.", "Google Fonts (fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com) serves the app's typefaces. Google Books (books.google.com) serves covers and the preview, and sets the cookies described above.", "The Internet Archive (archive.org) streams LibriVox recordings and audio clips. Termly (app.termly.io) serves the consent banner.", "When you pay, you go to Stripe's own checkout page, where Stripe sets its own cookies under its privacy policy. We never see your card details.", "OpenDyslexic, the reading font, is part of the app itself, so choosing it sends nothing to anyone."]}, {"heading": "Do my choices apply on all my devices?", "paragraphs": ["No. Cookie settings you make in your browser, and anything you clear there, apply to that browser on that device only. You'll need to make them again on a different device or browser, and a private or incognito window deletes what it kept when you close it.", "Clearing LiteraryWorm's site data signs you out, and books saved for offline will need saving again."]}, {"heading": "How can I control cookies on my browser?", "paragraphs": ["As the means by which you can refuse cookies through your web browser controls vary from browser to browser, you should visit your browser's help menu for more information.", "That's true of the most popular browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge and Opera. In each, you can block third-party cookies for every site, or clear the cookies and site data of one site.", "We don't use advertising networks, so there's nothing to opt out of here. If you'd like to opt out of targeted advertising elsewhere, most advertising networks offer a way to: see the Digital Advertising Alliance, the Digital Advertising Alliance of Canada or the European Interactive Digital Advertising Alliance."]}, {"heading": "Local network access", "paragraphs": ["Your browser may ask whether LiteraryWorm can reach devices on your local network, such as others on your home Wi-Fi.", "Choose Block: the app never needs it, and allowing it can stop logging in from working in that browser. If you allowed it, turn it off in the site's settings (in Chrome and Edge, select the icon beside the address, then Site settings, and set Local network access to Block)."]}, {"heading": "What about other tracking technologies, like web beacons?", "paragraphs": ["Cookies are not the only way to recognize or track visitors to a website. Web beacons (sometimes called \"tracking pixels\" or \"clear gifs\") are tiny graphics files that contain a unique identifier that lets a website recognize when someone has visited it or opened an email including them.", "LiteraryWorm doesn't use web beacons or tracking pixels on the Website or in its emails. We send our emails with Mailgun's open and click tracking turned off."]}, {"heading": "Do you serve targeted advertising?", "paragraphs": ["No. We don't serve advertising on our Website, and we don't allow third parties to place cookies or web beacons on your computer or mobile device through our Website to serve or measure advertising. Google's cookies from books.google.com are set under Google's own policies; we don't use them, and we don't receive them."]}, {"heading": "How often will you update this Cookie Policy?", "paragraphs": ["We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time in order to reflect, for example, changes to the cookies we use or for other operational, legal, or regulatory reasons. Please therefore revisit this Cookie Policy regularly to stay informed about our use of cookies and related technologies.", "The Last updated date at the top of this Cookie Policy shows when it last changed. When a change matters, we'll also say so on What's new."]}, {"heading": "Where can I get further information?", "paragraphs": ["If you have any questions about our use of cookies or other technologies, please email us at support@literaryworm.com. For privacy requests, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile lives inside your account. Only you, the account holder, can create one, and only after you consent.", "It keeps what it needs to work: a first name or nickname, an avatar and the child's reading. We never ask a child for an email address, full name, photo, location or any way to contact them.", "Its reading is private to your account. It isn't shown to other members, it isn't used for advertising, and it is never sold, rented or licensed.", "You can see it, download it, change its limits or delete it at any time from Account."]}, {"heading": "Your consent comes first", "paragraphs": ["Only the account holder, who must be 18 or older, can create a Kids profile or move a profile to Kids. You do it after reading this notice, and you confirm it with the account password.", "We keep a record of that consent: when it was given, how, and which version of this notice it was for.", "Moving the profile to another age rating, or deleting it, withdraws that consent, and we record that too."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile collects", "paragraphs": ["The profile: its first name or nickname, its avatar, its age rating, and any daily reading limit, weekly reading goal and bedtime you set.", "Its reading: the books in its library, where it is in each book, its bookmarks, highlights and notes, its Up next queue, ratings, the moods and pace it tags books with, favourites and lists, the authors and narrators it follows, and its release reminders.", "Its time: how long it reads and listens each day, in total and for each book (shown on the book's page), the books it finishes, its reading goals and pace, and any reading plan it makes (the day it chose to finish by and where it was when the plan started).", "Its learning: the words it saves from the dictionary and when they're next due for review, its private reading journal, and its chapter quiz scores.", "Its family activity: the books it asks a grown-up for and your answers, and the household challenges it starts or joins, which the other profiles on your account can see.", "Badges are worked out on the device from this reading and are never stored. Books saved for offline reading stay on that device."]}, {"heading": "What we never collect", "paragraphs": ["We don't ask a child for their email address, full name, home address, school, phone number, photo, voice, location or any other way to contact them.", "A Kids profile can't write anything that other members see, so it can't share personal details with them.", "There's no advertising on LiteraryWorm and no advertising trackers. Our visit counter, Ahrefs Web Analytics, is switched off while a Kids profile is in use, so nothing a child does there is sent to it.", "Kids profiles show only LiteraryWorm's own titles, so Google Books covers and previews, and the third-party cookies Google sets from books.google.com with them, don't load there."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile can't do", "paragraphs": ["Kids profiles see only books rated for children. A grown-up can say yes to a book above that rating when the child asks for it.", "They can't write public reading logs, join or start book clubs, follow other readers, share lists by link, upload or import books, search Google Books, ask the book's AI assistant, translate passages or use Who's who.", "They can't make purchases or change account settings. A grown-up's password is needed to open Account or to allow extra time past a daily limit."]}, {"heading": "AI features", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile can read AI-written book summaries and content notes, hear a recap of earlier chapters (Previously…) and take chapter quizzes. These are written by Claude, made by Anthropic.", "We send Anthropic only the book's details or its own text and which chapter it's about, never the child's name, answers, scores or anything else about them. The summaries, content notes, recaps and quizzes are kept and shared with every reader of that book, so they say nothing about who asked."]}, {"heading": "Who sees it", "paragraphs": ["You do: Account → Family shows each Kids profile's last 7 days, its weekly goal, its book requests and its quiz scores.", "If you turn on the weekly Kids reading report, we email last week's reading to your account's email address. Mailgun sends it for us. It's off until you turn it on.", "Our hosting providers, Supabase and Vercel, store and serve it only to run LiteraryWorm for you.", "Our support team can see how many profiles an account has, but not a profile's name, library, reading, notes or journal."]}, {"heading": "How long we keep it", "paragraphs": ["We keep a Kids profile's information for as long as the profile exists.", "Deleting the profile, or your whole account, deletes everything it collected from our database straight away. Copies in our providers' backups are removed when those backups expire."]}, {"heading": "Your choices as a parent", "paragraphs": ["From Account you can see the profile's activity, download a copy of your data, change its daily limit, weekly goal, bedtime and age rating, and answer its book requests.", "You can add a PIN to the other profiles so a child can't open them.", "You can stop us collecting anything more at any time by deleting the profile, which deletes everything it collected. Moving it to another age rating also ends the Kids protections, but keeps its reading under its new rating."]}, {"heading": "Keeping it safe", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile's information is stored with access rules, so only your account can read it. Our support team can't see a profile's name, library or reading.", "You can protect the account with two-step sign-in or a passkey, and lock other profiles with a PIN, which we keep only as a one-way hash."]}, {"heading": "Changes to this notice", "paragraphs": ["We keep the version of this notice you agreed to with each Kids profile. If we change what a Kids profile collects, we'll update this notice and say so on What's new."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["If you have a question about your child's information, or think a child is using LiteraryWorm without a parent's consent, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com. We'll answer, and we'll delete information collected without consent.", "The Privacy Policy explains how we handle everyone's information, including your rights where you live."]}]$lw$::jsonb, updated_at = now()
