ivity: the books it asks a grown-up for and your answers, and the household challenges it starts or joins, which the other profiles on your account can see.", "Badges are worked out on the device from this reading and are never stored. Books saved for offline reading stay on that device."]}, {"heading": "What we never collect", "paragraphs": ["We don't ask a child for their email address, full name, home address, school, phone number, photo, voice, location or any other way to contact them.", "A Kids profile can't write anything that other members see, so it can't share personal details with them.", "There's no advertising on LiteraryWorm, and we don't use analytics or advertising trackers.", "Kids profiles show only LiteraryWorm's own titles, so Google Books covers and previews, and the third-party cookies Google sets from books.google.com with them, don't load there."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile can't do", "paragraphs": ["Kids profiles see only books rated for children. A grown-up can say yes to a book above that rating when the child asks for it.", "They can't write public reading logs, join or start book clubs, follow other readers, share lists by link, upload or import books, search Google Books, ask the book's AI assistant, translate passages or use Who's who.", "They can't make purchases or change account settings. A grown-up's password is needed to open Account or to allow extra time past a daily limit."]}, {"heading": "AI features", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile can read AI-written book summaries and content notes, hear a recap of earlier chapters (Previously…) and take chapter quizzes. These are written by Claude, made by Anthropic.", "We send Anthropic only the book's details or its own text and which chapter it's about, never the child's name, answers, scores or anything else about them. The summaries, content notes, recaps and quizzes are kept and shared with every reader of that book, so they say nothing about who asked."]}, {"heading": "Who sees it", "paragraphs": ["You do: Account → Family shows each Kids profile's last 7 days, its weekly goal, its book requests and its quiz scores.", "If you turn on the weekly Kids reading report, we email last week's reading to your account's email address. Mailgun sends it for us. It's off until you turn it on.", "Our hosting providers, Supabase and Vercel, store and serve it only to run LiteraryWorm for you.", "Our support team can see how many profiles an account has, but not a profile's name, library, reading, notes or journal."]}, {"heading": "How long we keep it", "paragraphs": ["We keep a Kids profile's information for as long as the profile exists.", "Deleting the profile, or your whole account, deletes everything it collected from our database straight away. Copies in our providers' backups are removed when those backups expire."]}, {"heading": "Your choices as a parent", "paragraphs": ["From Account you can see the profile's activity, download a copy of your data, change its daily limit, weekly goal, bedtime and age rating, and answer its book requests.", "You can add a PIN to the other profiles so a child can't open them.", "You can stop us collecting anything more at any time by deleting the profile, which deletes everything it collected. Moving it to another age rating also ends the Kids protections, but keeps its reading under its new rating."]}, {"heading": "Keeping it safe", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile's information is stored with access rules, so only your account can read it. Our support team can't see a profile's name, library or reading.", "You can protect the account with two-step sign-in or a passkey, and lock other profiles with a PIN, which we keep only as a one-way hash."]}, {"heading": "Changes to this notice", "paragraphs": ["We keep the version of this notice you agreed to with each Kids profile. If we change what a Kids profile collects, we'll update this notice and say so on What's new."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["If you have a question about your child's information, or think a child is using LiteraryWorm without a parent's consent, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com. We'll answer, and we'll delete information collected without consent.", "The Privacy Policy explains how we handle everyone's information, including your rights where you live."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["We don't sell, rent or license your personal information, and we don't share it for advertising. There's nothing to opt out of there, and Global Privacy Control is honoured.", "You decide which emails and notifications you get, what your browser keeps, what other members see, and whether your data stays. You can change each of these in Account at any time."]}, {"heading": "Selling and sharing", "paragraphs": ["We don't sell, rent or license your personal information, and we don't share it for cross-context behavioural advertising.", "If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a request to opt out. Nothing changes, because we already don't do either."]}, {"heading": "Emails", "paragraphs": ["In Account → Preferences, turn each kind of email on or off: books you set Remind me on coming out, new books from authors you follow, club meeting reminders and changes, a daily email of new club posts, the weekly Kids reading report, the monthly What's new, and marketing emails. Several are off until you turn them on.", "Each of these emails has an unsubscribe link that works in one click. Emails about your account, such as confirming your address or resetting your password, always arrive."]}, {"heading": "Notifications on your devices", "paragraphs": ["Notifications on this device, in Account → Preferences, are off until you turn them on, and are set for each device. Choose which ones you get: books coming out, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, the evening streak nudge and answers to Kids book requests.", "Logging out on a device turns them off there. Each book club also has its own alerts switch on its page."]}, {"heading": "Cookies and browser storage", "paragraphs": ["We set no advertising or analytics cookies. Our backend's host, Cloudflare, sets one cookie to keep out bots, and Google sets third-party cookies from books.google.com when Google Books covers and previews load, because we use the Google Books API.", "Analytics: if you allow it in the consent banner, Ahrefs Web Analytics counts the pages you visit, without cookies. To turn it off, choose Consent Preferences at the bottom of any page and decline analytics. It never runs for Kids profiles.", "Change your cookie choice with Consent Preferences at the bottom of every page, and block third-party cookies in your browser to stop Google's. The Cookie Policy lists everything your browser keeps and how to clear it."]}, {"heading": "What other members see", "paragraphs": ["Your library, progress, notes, highlights, journal, moods and saved words are private to your household. Reading logs you publish show on the book's page with your display name.", "Your reader page, which gathers your public reading logs, is off until you turn it on, and turning it off removes its followers. In each book club, Show my place is off until you turn it on."]}, {"heading": "Your data", "paragraphs": ["In Account you can download a copy of your data, correct your display name, and delete profiles or your whole account.", "Reading logs, club posts, shared highlights, saved words, journal entries and uploads can each be deleted whenever you like. The Privacy Policy explains what we keep and for how long."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["Email usprivacy@literaryworm.com with any question about your privacy choices, or to make a request under the law where you live."]}]$lw$::jsonb, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$privacy-choices$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["We don't sell, rent or license your personal information, and we don't share it for advertising. There's nothing to opt out of there, and Global Privacy Control is honoured.", "You decide which emails and notifications you get, what your browser keeps, what other members see, and whether your data stays. You can change each of these in Account at any time."]}, {"heading": "Selling and sharing", "paragraphs": ["We don't sell, rent or license your personal information, and we don't share it for cross-context behavioural advertising.", "If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a request to opt out. Nothing changes, because we already don't do either."]}, {"heading": "Emails", "paragraphs": ["In Account → Preferences, turn each kind of email on or off: books you set Remind me on coming out, new books from authors you follow, club meeting reminders and changes, a daily email of new club posts, the weekly Kids reading report, the monthly What's new, and marketing emails. Several are off until you turn them on.", "Each of these emails has an unsubscribe link that works in one click. Emails about your account, such as confirming your address or resetting your password, always arrive."]}, {"heading": "Notifications on your devices", "paragraphs": ["Notifications on this device, in Account → Preferences, are off until you turn them on, and are set for each device. Choose which ones you get: books coming out, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, the evening streak nudge and answers to Kids book requests.", "Logging out on a device turns them off there. Each book club also has its own alerts switch on its page."]}, {"heading": "Cookies and browser storage", "paragraphs": ["We set no advertising or analytics cookies. Our backend's host, Cloudflare, sets one cookie to keep out bots, and Google sets third-party cookies from books.google.com when Google Books covers and previews load, because we use the Google Books API.", "Change your cookie choice with Consent Preferences at the bottom of every page, and block third-party cookies in your browser to stop Google's. The Cookie Policy lists everything your browser keeps and how to clear it."]}, {"heading": "What other members see", "paragraphs": ["Your library, progress, notes, highlights, journal, moods and saved words are private to your household. Reading logs you publish show on the book's page with your display name.", "Your reader page, which gathers your public reading logs, is off until you turn it on, and turning it off removes its followers. In each book club, Show my place is off until you turn it on."]}, {"heading": "Your data", "paragraphs": ["In Account you can download a copy of your data, correct your display name, and delete profiles or your whole account.", "Reading logs, club posts, shared highlights, saved words, journal entries and uploads can each be deleted whenever you like. The Privacy Policy explains what we keep and for how long."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["Email usprivacy@literaryworm.com with any question about your privacy choices, or to make a request under the law where you live."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

insert into public.changelog_entries (released_on, version, kind, title, body, major)
select '2026-11-02'::date, '2026.11', 'update', $lw$Counting visits with Ahrefs Web Analytics$lw$, $lw$If you allow analytics in the consent banner, Ahrefs Web Analytics counts the pages people visit, so we can see what's used. It sets no cookies, page addresses go without search words or codes, and it never runs for Kids profiles or on pages with codes in their links. The Privacy Policy, Cookie Policy, Children's Privacy Notice and Your Privacy Choices say so.$lw$, false
where not exists (select 1 from public.changelog_entries c where c.title = $lw$Counting visits with Ahrefs Web Analytics$lw$ and c.version = '2026.11');
